From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] winegstreamer: media sink characteristics, presentation clock, stream removal, stream sink markers / flush / type handler

The MPEG-4 / MP3 media sink's stubs, as the Media Foundation documentation and
mf's test_mpeg4_media_sink() have them:

- GetCharacteristics: MEDIASINK_RATELESS (E_POINTER for NULL, MF_E_SHUTDOWN
  after Shutdown); IMFGetService on the sink (no services).
- Set/GetPresentationClock: the sink registers as a clock state sink with the
  clock, a new clock replaces the old, NULL detaches, MF_E_NO_CLOCK when none,
  Shutdown detaches, MF_E_SHUTDOWN afterwards. OnClockSetRate: S_OK (rateless).
- RemoveStreamSink: MF_E_INVALIDSTREAMNUMBER for an unknown id; the muxer
  cannot drop a stream, so a new muxer is built from the remaining streams
  (before the sink was started; MF_E_INVALIDREQUEST after). The removed stream
  sink answers MF_E_STREAMSINK_REMOVED. AddStreamSink / GetStreamSinkCount /
  ByIndex / ById answer MF_E_SHUTDOWN after Shutdown, AddStreamSink clears its
  output and refuses a NULL type (E_POINTER) instead of crashing.
- Stream sink PlaceMarker: goes through the sample queue and raises
  MEStreamSinkMarker (with the context) once reached. Flush: queued samples
  are dropped, queued markers are still signalled. Both give
  MF_E_STREAMSINK_REMOVED when removed / shut down.
- Stream sink media type handler: GetMajorType, GetMediaTypeCount (1),
  GetMediaTypeByIndex (a copy of the type, MF_E_NO_MORE_TYPES), 
  IsMediaTypeSupported (same major type and subtype, else
  MF_E_INVALIDMEDIATYPE), SetCurrentMediaType (the muxer is rebuilt with the
  new type, before start).
- The async callback GetParameters E_NOTIMPL (use the queue's defaults) is
  documented, no FIXME there.

mf's test_mpeg4_media_sink() loses its 19 todo_wine marks.

---diff --git a/dlls/winegstreamer/media_sink.c b/dlls/winegstreamer/media_sink.c
